// Corpus for handoff-self-monitoring/lib/handoff.js - scan().
// A decision named but not handed off: an offer ("let me know", "should I"),
// or a fork stated without a default, in a closing message with no [HANDOFF]
// block. A close that already carries a well-formed block must not fire.

{"text": "The parser is done. Let me know if you want the streaming path too.", "expect": "hit", "why": "offer: let me know"}
{"text": "Tests pass. If you'd like, I can also wire the retries.", "expect": "hit", "why": "offer: if you would like"}
{"text": "Migration written. Would you like me to run it against staging?", "expect": "hit", "why": "offer: would you like me to"}
{"text": "I fixed the leak. Should I also bump the dependency?", "expect": "hit", "why": "offer: should I"}
{"text": "Refactor complete. Want me to split it into two commits?", "expect": "hit", "why": "offer: want me to"}
{"text": "Both approaches work - up to you.", "expect": "hit", "why": "offer: up to you"}
{"text": "I can use a queue or a cron. Your call.", "expect": "hit", "why": "offer: your call"}
{"text": "Done. Happy to switch it to a worker pool instead.", "expect": "hit", "why": "offer: happy to switch"}
{"text": "Which one to pick depends on whether you need ordering guarantees.", "expect": "hit", "why": "fork: depends on"}
{"text": "I used a mutex. Alternatively, a channel would work.", "expect": "hit", "why": "fork: alternatively"}
{"text": "The other option is to denormalize the table.", "expect": "hit", "why": "fork: the other option"}
{"text": "There are three approaches to this caching problem.", "expect": "hit", "why": "fork: three approaches"}
{"text": "Option A is faster; option B is simpler to review.", "expect": "hit", "why": "fork: option A / B"}
{"text": "There are real trade-offs between the two designs.", "expect": "hit", "why": "fork: trade-offs"}
{"text": "We could either batch the writes or widen the lock.", "expect": "hit", "why": "fork: could either"}
{"text": "Which would you prefer for the retry backoff?", "expect": "hit", "why": "fork: which would you prefer"}

// --- must NOT fire ---

{"text": "Done. All 66 tests pass; the parser now handles chunked input.", "expect": "miss", "why": "a plain close with no fork and no offer"}
{"text": "The build is broken: `npm ci` fails with ENOSPC. I cleared the cache and it passes now.", "expect": "miss", "why": "a report, not a decision"}
{"text": "I used a mutex because the channel version deadlocked under the load test.\n\n[HANDOFF]\n- Status: done\n- Situation: the writer no longer deadlocks; throughput is unchanged\n- Next: nothing", "expect": "miss", "why": "a well-formed block, status done"}
{"text": "Both approaches work.\n\n[HANDOFF]\n- Status: needs-decision\n- Situation: the queue is written but not wired; either transport works\n- Options:\n  - Redis: one less service, loses messages on restart\n  - SQS: durable, adds an AWS dependency\n  - Default: Redis - the restart window is already covered by the replay log\n- Next: tell me which transport and I will wire it", "expect": "miss", "why": "a fork WITH options and a default is exactly what the skill asks for"}
{"text": "The `should I` phrasing is what the offer detector looks for.", "expect": "miss", "why": "inline code is stripped"}
{"text": "> Let me know if you want the streaming path too.", "expect": "miss", "why": "quoted lines are stripped"}
{"text": "I let the user know that the migration had run.", "expect": "miss", "why": "the offer pattern is the fixed phrase 'let me know'; an object in between is a report, not an offer"}

// --- probes for the object-anchored "depends on" pattern ---

{"text": "The scheduler depends on lodash and date-fns.", "expect": "miss", "why": "a package dependency, not a fork"}
{"text": "This module depends on node 22.", "expect": "miss", "why": "a runtime dependency - note 'This depends on' would have fired on the adjacent-pronoun pattern, the object is what saves it"}
{"text": "Build order depends on the topological sort.", "expect": "miss", "why": "an explanation of a relationship"}
{"text": "The retry count depends on your config file, which I did not change.", "expect": "miss", "why": "'depends on your' is explanatory; only whether|which|what|if count as a choice"}
{"text": "Throughput depends on how many workers you run.", "expect": "miss", "why": "'depends on how' is explanatory"}
{"text": "Which transport to use depends on whether you need durability.", "expect": "hit", "why": "a fork with a choice-shaped object and no default named"}
{"text": "Whether to batch depends on what your p99 target is.", "expect": "hit", "why": "choice-shaped object"}
{"text": "Which transport to use depends on whether you need durability.\n\n[HANDOFF]\n- Status: needs-decision\n- Situation: the queue is written, either transport drops in\n- Options:\n  - SQS: durable, +40ms\n  - Redis: in-stack, loses on restart\n  - Default: SQS - the replay log does not cover a cold start\n- Next: confirm SQS and I will wire it", "expect": "miss", "why": "the same fork WITH options and a default is what the skill asks for"}

// --- a block the agent decorated (bold or heading) is still a block ---

{"text": "Both transports work - let me know which you prefer.\n\n**[HANDOFF]**\n- Status: needs-decision\n- Situation: the queue is written, either transport drops in\n- Options:\n  - SQS: durable, +40ms\n  - Redis: in-stack, loses on restart\n  - Default: SQS - the replay log does not cover a cold start\n- Next: confirm SQS and I will wire it", "expect": "miss", "why": "a bolded marker is the same block"}
{"text": "Done, though it depends on whether you need ordering.\n\n## [HANDOFF]\n- Status: done\n- Situation: the writer no longer deadlocks\n- Next: nothing", "expect": "miss", "why": "heading marker"}
{"text": "Should I also bump the dependency? The format is `**[HANDOFF]**` followed by the fields.", "expect": "hit", "why": "a decorated marker in inline code is documentation - the offer stands unhanded"}

// --- a FENCED example of the block is documentation, not a handoff ---

{"text": "Should I also bump the dependency?\n\nThe format is:\n\n```\n[HANDOFF]\n- Status: done\n- Situation: <one sentence>\n- Next: nothing\n```\n\nThat is the shape.", "expect": "hit", "why": "a fenced template does not hand off the offer"}
{"text": "Done. All tests pass.\n\nFor reference, the format is:\n\n```\n[HANDOFF]\n- Status: <done | needs-decision | blocked>\n- Situation: <one sentence in the reader's terms>\n- Next: <one action, or nothing>\n```\n\nThat is the shape.", "expect": "miss", "why": "documenting the format, with no offer and no fork - a fenced template must not be judged as a declared block"}
{"text": "**[HANDOFF]**\n- **Status:** done\n- **Situation:** the installed trees match the repo\n- **Next:** start the migration", "expect": "miss", "why": "decorated field names are the same fields - found by writing one, not by the eval"}
{"text": "[HANDOFF]\n- __Status__: needs-decision\n- __Situation__: two transports are viable\n- __Options__:\n  - A: Redis - already running\n  - B: SQS - managed durability\n- __Default__: A, because the log already covers restart loss\n- __Next__: reply A or B", "expect": "miss", "why": "underscore emphasis, and Options sub-items still parse under a decorated Options line"}

// --- a phrase in double quotes is cited, not said ---
// Measured in a real session: an A/B table quoting the detector's own trigger
// phrases drew a retrospective for a close that offered nothing.
{"text":"| Case | Result |\n|---|---|\n| handoff EN: \"If you want, I can also... Should I proceed?\" | detects offer and fork |\n| handoff ES | detects only the question |\n\nThe detectors are English-only.","expect":"miss","why":"the offer is quoted inside a table cell - a citation, not a handoff"}
{"text":"The corpus now covers “let me know” and “should I”, both as hits.","expect":"miss","why":"curly-quoted phrases are citations"}
